    "moka_reviews": {
      "type": "testimonials",
      "blocks": {
        "moka_rev_1": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "star_rating": 5,
            "title": "",
            "text": "<p>I work with infants and have taken apart every annoying bottle known to man. Dr Brown's are the ones I least want to see in a bag because of all the pieces and leaking if they tip. Moka is much more straightforward. My own baby feeds well from it and I can actually clean it properly.</p>",
            "author": "Hannah Stewart · Verified"
          }
        },
        "moka_rev_2": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "star_rating": 5,
            "title": "",
            "text": "<p>We wasted money on Pigeon, Comotomo and two Dr Brown's sizes before this. The others were not terrible, they just didn't fit my baby. Moka is pricey, but if I had bought one of these first instead of a bunch of maybes I would have saved money.</p>",
            "author": "Priya Shah · Verified"
          }
        },
        "moka_rev_3": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "star_rating": 5,
            "title": "",
            "text": "<p>We were a Dr. Brown's house because my daughter was so gassy after feeds. Moka has been the first bottle that gives us the same calm feed vibe without me standing at the sink with a little brush for 20 minutes. She is not gulping air like before.</p>",
            "author": "Megan Carter · Verified"
          }
        },
        "moka_rev_4": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "star_rating": 4,
            "title": "",
            "text": "<p>I love the glass and the simple parts. Baby took it right away after rejecting Tommee Tippee. Only downside is that it is heavier than our plastic bottles, so I wouldn't hand it to a baby to hold alone. For supervised feeds it is perfect.</p>",
            "author": "Sarah Coleman · Verified"
          }
        },
        "moka_rev_5": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "star_rating": 5,
            "title": "",
            "text": "<p>I'm the dad who handles the middle-of-the-night bottle, and I care if it leaks and if I can clean it half asleep. This is way easier than the Dr Brown's setup we had. Fewer parts, markings are easy to see, and I haven't had milk running down my wrist at 3am.</p>",
            "author": "Ryan Miller · Verified"
          }
        },
        "moka_rev_6": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "star_rating": 5,
            "title": "",
            "text": "<p>I went down the microplastics rabbit hole after using plastic Dr Browns with my oldest. For this baby I wanted glass, but not a bottle that felt like a mason jar experiment. Moka was the best middle ground I found: glass body, simple parts, still anti-colic style.</p>",
            "author": "Rachel Kim · Verified"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "moka_rev_1",
        "moka_rev_2",
        "moka_rev_3",
        "moka_rev_4",
        "moka_rev_5",
        "moka_rev_6"
      ],
